    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d10-a2">

                <pb facs="0105" n="11" sameAs="frus:frus1887/pg11"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 75.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hanna to Mr. Costa</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Buenos Ayres</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-03-12"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 12,
                        1887</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Minister</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge
                    the receipt of your communication of the 10th instant, furnishing the joyful
                    intelligence that the cholera epidemic has disappeared from your shores, and
                    that ships leaving Argentine ports would be given clean bills of health.</p>
                <p>These facts will be at once transmitted to my Government, and I assure you the
                    intelligence will cause very widespread rejoicing.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bayless W. Hanna.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
